  "body": "There's a separate [issue](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/4516) for adapting the whatwg/html spec.\r\n\r\nWhen a label has an associated [labeled control](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#labeled-control), the [dispatch algorithm](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-dispatch) should adjust the target to the labeled control. See for instance the first example at https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-label-element. It seems this would match the behavior of at least Firefox, Chrome and Safari (tested on Windows, Ubuntu and OSX -- obviously, where the OS supports the browser).\r\n\r\nE.g.:\r\n```\r\ndata:text/html,<label id=\"cb-label\">CB <input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"cb\"></label> <script> e = new MouseEvent(\"click\"); document.getElementById(\"cb-label\").dispatchEvent(e); </script>\r\n```",
